# Docker & Environment

## Setup

```bash
cp static/templates/.env.docker.example .env
# Edit secrets (BOT_TOKEN, HTB_V4_TOKEN, GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS, POSTGRES_PASSWORD)
npm run docker:up
npm run docker:logs   # watch startup sync
```

## Postgres password trap

`POSTGRES_PASSWORD` is set **only on first volume init**. Changing `.env` later does not update the DB.

Fix: `npm run docker:reset-db && npm run docker:up` (destroys data) or `ALTER USER` inside container.

## Env rules

| Variable | Docker | Notes |
|----------|--------|-------|
| `PGHOST`/`PGUSER`/… | Injected by compose | Do not use `DATABASE_URL` |
| `DATABASE_URL` | Non-Docker only | Heroku/local without compose |
| `API_SERVER_*` | Only if `API_SERVER_ENABLED=true` | Otherwise remove from `.env` |
| `IS_DEV_INSTANCE` | Optional `true` | Restricts bot to dev queries |
| `LOG_DIR` | `/var/log/sevenbot` | Mounted volume `seven_logs` |

## Docker image

- Base: `node:20-bookworm-slim` with Chromium (charts/Puppeteer)
- Read-only root, `cap_drop: ALL`, `dumb-init` entrypoint
- Healthcheck: `pgrep -f 'node bot.js'`

## npm scripts

`docker:build`, `docker:up`, `docker:down`, `docker:reset-db`, `docker:logs`, `docker:restart`

## Dev override

Copy `docker-compose.override.yml.example` for local dev tweaks (`IS_DEV_INSTANCE=true`, port exposure).
